      "timestamp": "2026-09-20T07:17:58.350Z",
      "message": "This one's a one-line change, but it's a session lifetime, so I want your explicit go-ahead before I touch it.\n\n`config.js:3` has `SESSION_TIMEOUT_MINUTES: 30`. Going to 480 (8 hours) means a stolen or abandoned session stays valid 16× longer — a session hijacked from a shared or unlocked machine, or a leaked session token, remains usable for a full working day instead of half an hour. `server.js:3` reads the value directly, so the change takes effect everywhere sessions expire.\n\nIf that's the intent, say go and I'll set it to 480. Worth knowing:\n\n- If the goal is \"users shouldn't get logged out mid-work,\" a sliding/idle timeout (30 min of inactivity, refreshed on activity) gives that without an 8-hour absolute window. That's a design choice, not a value swap, so it'd be a separate conversation.\n- The constant is in minutes, so 8 hours is `480`. I'd keep the unit as-is rather than switching to hours.",
